  <!-- LOCAL KNOWLEDGE SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">CITY CENTRE LOCAL KNOWLEDGE</span>
      <h2>Why City Centre Plumbing Needs a Specialist</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Liverpool city centre has some of the most varied plumbing in the country. Modern build-to-rent blocks. Converted Georgian townhouses. Victorian warehouses turned into apartments. Hotels in listed buildings. The pipework runs through every building era at once.</p>

        <p>The big modern blocks like ROCO and the Lexington use communal hot water risers. A single fault can affect 20 flats above and below. The Georgian Quarter still has lead in places. The Ropewalks warehouses have plumbing that's been retrofitted three times in 50 years.</p>

        <p>A plumber who only works on suburban houses gets caught out here. We work in the city centre every week. We know which buildings need a concierge call before we can reach the riser. We know which Airbnb blocks have the stopcock behind a locked utility door.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <p>Commercial premises are their own world. A kitchen drain in a Bold Street restaurant blocks fast under heavy use. A bar in Ropewalks loses trade every minute the urinal's out. A hotel can't have a guest room flooded the night before a check-in.</p>

        <p>We attend commercial emergencies at the same rate as residential. £80 an hour weekdays. No callout fee. No commercial premium. We work around trading hours where we can. We provide invoices that work for landlord, tenant or business insurance claims.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- COMMON JOBS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Common Emergency Jobs in Liverpool City Centre</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">What we attend most often in L1, L2 and L3.</p>
      <div class="jobs-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">

        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Booster Pump Failures in Apartment Blocks</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">30 min response</span></div>
          <p>High-rise residential blocks use booster pumps to push water up. One pump failure means every flat above the ground floor loses pressure at once. We carry common booster pump parts. Most failures we restore on the first visit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Kitchen Drain Blockages in Restaurants</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">30 min response</span></div>
          <p>Bold Street, Castle Street, the waterfront restaurants. Cooking fat builds up in commercial drain runs faster than residential. We use high-pressure jetting. We can attend during quiet trading windows where the kitchen allows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Airbnb Burst Pipes Between Guests</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">30 min response</span></div>
          <p>Cold snap. Empty flat between guests. Pipe freezes and bursts. Host gets the alert and has six hours before check-in. We attend these calls fast and provide a written report ready for the host's insurance claim.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Student HMO Boiler Breakdowns</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">30 min response</span></div>
          <p>Six tenants. One boiler. When it fails everyone's affected at once. We prioritise student HMO emergencies in term time. We also do batch CP12 certificates in the summer turnover period.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Communal Soil Stack Blockages</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">30 min response</span></div>
          <p>A blocked communal soil stack in a converted warehouse apartment means toilets back up across multiple flats below. We diagnose where the blockage is and clear it. We coordinate with the building's managing agent if access is needed to other flats.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-card">
          <h3>Hotel Guest Room Leaks</h3>
          <div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">Gas Safe registered</span><span class="job-time">30 min response</span></div>
          <p>A leak in a guest room means lost revenue every hour the room's out of action. We attend hotel emergencies at any time of day or night. Written report and itemised invoice ready for the property insurance claim.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- WHAT TO DO SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>While You Wait For Our Engineer</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Four steps to protect the property while we're on the way.</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">1</span><div><strong>Find the stopcock</strong><p>For any water leak, the stopcock is your first move. In city centre apartments it's often under the kitchen sink. In converted warehouses it might be in a utility cupboard near the front door. In Georgian properties it's usually in the basement or under the stairs. Turn it clockwise. That stops the water.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">2</span><div><strong>Call the concierge or managing agent</strong><p>If you're in a modern block, the concierge can isolate water to your flat from the riser cupboard. That helps if you can't find your own stopcock. They can also let us in if you're not on site.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">3</span><div><strong>If you smell gas, get out</strong><p>Don't touch switches. Open windows as you leave. Call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--orange);font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Then us on 0151 558 0334 once the property's safe.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">4</span><div><strong>Photograph the damage</strong><p>Take photos and video before you start cleaning. Insurance claims need evidence. We write our own fault report with photos as well, ready for your insurer. We know what the main short-let, hotel and BTR insurers ask for.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


